   "text": "Why these documents: they set out what the information program in Asia was for and how its first managers judged it. The thread runs from Jessup's call for an expanded program in 1949, through the Psychological Strategy Board's country-by-country plan and Saigon's 1952 effectiveness report, to the National Security Council's candid annual reports of 1955 and 1957."
